WEBVTT

00:02.450 --> 00:06.270
Am I auditioning, too?

00:07.390 --> 00:08.970
Some information on college.

00:08.970 --> 00:10.680
You ought to skim through it.

01:42.440 --> 01:44.500
<i>Auditions are coming.</i>

01:43.830 --> 01:46.620
Exec Notes

01:44.500 --> 01:48.310
<i>People would talk if the 
executives failed the auditions, right?</i>

01:46.620 --> 01:48.250
People would talk if the 
executives failed the auditions, right?

01:48.250 --> 01:49.380
You're stupid.

01:48.310 --> 01:49.370
<i>You're stupid.</i>

01:50.660 --> 01:53.000
The photos from the Agata Festival.

01:53.000 --> 01:54.930
They came out nice.

01:54.920 --> 01:56.170
It's okay.

01:54.930 --> 01:56.660
<i>It's okay.</i>

01:56.660 --> 01:59.450
<i>This is the only place the execs can rant.</i>

01:59.450 --> 02:00.860
<i>Cut him some slack.</i>

02:00.860 --> 02:02.160
Kumiko-chan.

02:02.630 --> 02:04.280
The photos are done.

02:04.280 --> 02:05.110
Really?

02:05.110 --> 02:06.480
The photos from the school trip, too.

02:06.480 --> 02:08.010
I wanna see!

02:09.910 --> 02:11.830
They came out nice.

02:11.830 --> 02:13.140
Could you send them to me later?

02:13.490 --> 02:16.290
S-Sorry, they're film photos.

02:16.290 --> 02:17.570
I'll get copies made.

02:17.570 --> 02:18.800
Copies?

02:19.320 --> 02:23.360
Come to think of it, 
Mayu-senpai isn't in any of these.

02:23.670 --> 02:25.220
You're right.

02:26.570 --> 02:31.450
I don't like being in photos too much.

02:31.450 --> 02:33.430
I just like taking them.

02:35.460 --> 02:39.380
<b>Episode 6</b>

02:35.460 --> 02:39.380
<b>Wavering Dissonance</b>

02:50.030 --> 02:50.800
There.

02:51.780 --> 02:54.310
The triplets aren't together.

02:54.310 --> 02:56.860
Brass, listen to the winds carefully.

02:56.860 --> 02:57.580
Yes.

02:58.190 --> 03:03.500
<i>With the Agata Festival over,
 summer was upon us.</i>

03:02.380 --> 03:04.640
It's important to get in the groove,

03:04.120 --> 03:08.710
<i>A month remains until the 
concert band Prefecturals.</i>

03:04.640 --> 03:09.410
but don't waste all of your
breath on the accents.

03:09.410 --> 03:12.200
Be mindful when you pass the 
melody onto the trumpets.

03:12.580 --> 03:13.700
Yes.

03:22.770 --> 03:27.740
There's no point trying to tune your 
instrument by changing your embouchure.

03:27.740 --> 03:29.650
Really?

03:29.650 --> 03:34.600
You have to adjust the instrument itself so 
that it's in tune when you're blowing normally.

03:34.600 --> 03:35.710
I see.

03:35.710 --> 03:37.410
Once you get it tuned right,

03:37.410 --> 03:43.480
you have to memorize what that sounds like 
and learn to notice when it's off-pitch.

03:44.460 --> 03:46.680
I'm never going to get it.

03:46.680 --> 03:47.230
Yeah...

03:47.590 --> 03:50.060
It takes a while.

03:50.060 --> 03:53.370
Even just being aware of when 
you get pitchy helps, though.

03:53.650 --> 03:55.260
I had no idea.

03:55.260 --> 03:57.460
Our senpais are amazing.

03:57.460 --> 03:59.220
These are fundamental skills.

03:59.220 --> 04:01.300
You have to learn them.

04:01.530 --> 04:02.370
Yeah.

04:02.910 --> 04:04.530
Hang in there, Kaho-chan.

04:04.530 --> 04:05.360
Right.

04:13.310 --> 04:14.600
Kanade-chan...

04:14.600 --> 04:15.340
Yes?

04:15.340 --> 04:17.810
That dotted quarter was short.

04:18.890 --> 04:20.400
Was it really?

04:20.400 --> 04:20.790
Yeah.

04:22.350 --> 04:24.160
Right...

04:24.160 --> 04:25.660
Thank you.

04:25.660 --> 04:27.350
That's our president.

04:27.350 --> 04:29.280
Sending gifts to the enemy.

04:29.280 --> 04:30.900
You're such a giving person.

04:31.690 --> 04:32.670
Enemy?

04:33.510 --> 04:34.480
Yes.

04:34.480 --> 04:36.580
The auditions are coming up.

04:36.580 --> 04:39.270
The clarinets are at each other's throats.

04:39.270 --> 04:42.340
Something about there being a new 
first-year that's really good.

04:42.340 --> 04:43.260
Of course.

04:45.670 --> 04:51.770
I still think I should drop out.

04:53.940 --> 04:56.130
You mentioned that before, too.

04:56.130 --> 04:59.350
You don't need more than 
two euphoniums, do you?

04:59.350 --> 05:01.030
You have the soli, too.

05:01.620 --> 05:07.600
I'd feel bad if I were chosen 
and someone had to sit out.

05:08.800 --> 05:12.080
So what you're saying is that you're certain

05:12.080 --> 05:15.450
you'd make the audition if 
you went through with it.

05:17.110 --> 05:19.950
No, that's not what I meant.

05:20.450 --> 05:21.400
But...

05:25.630 --> 05:26.810
Um...

05:26.810 --> 05:28.050
Mayu-chan...

05:29.430 --> 05:35.640
Sorry, I don't really understand 
why you would feel so bad.

05:36.320 --> 05:37.730
Don't you?

05:38.270 --> 05:40.470
It's like I said before.

05:40.470 --> 05:46.860
I'd feel guilty playing in place of
someone who's been at Kitauji all this time.

05:48.660 --> 05:51.260
I mean, I kind of get it.

05:51.650 --> 05:54.880
Especially if the president 
were to drop out.

05:54.880 --> 05:56.120
It would affect the club's...

05:56.120 --> 05:57.240
Kanade-chan!

05:58.990 --> 06:01.000
Umm...

06:01.290 --> 06:05.860
We audition to choose the best people for 
each part to participate in the competition.

06:05.860 --> 06:08.620
That's how it's always been at Kitauji.

06:08.620 --> 06:10.600
Are you opposed to that?

06:11.750 --> 06:13.960
I'm not opposed...

06:15.120 --> 06:19.320
But would anyone really be 
happy to see me chosen?

06:21.470 --> 06:22.280
Of course!

06:22.930 --> 06:23.600
Who?

06:25.280 --> 06:26.830
All the other members.

06:32.480 --> 06:35.750
Kitauji is going for national gold.

06:35.750 --> 06:39.040
So it doesn't matter what year you 
are or what you've been doing.

06:39.040 --> 06:41.210
We put our best forward to the competition.

06:41.740 --> 06:44.960
That's the best way to achieve our goal.

06:45.260 --> 06:49.470
That's why we chose to do it that way.

06:50.450 --> 06:53.460
Sorry, you're the president.

06:53.460 --> 06:55.360
That doesn't matter!

06:55.360 --> 06:57.110
Sorry.

06:57.110 --> 06:58.310
She's right.

06:58.310 --> 07:04.190
Kumiko-senpai was furious at everyone
who threw the audition last year.

07:04.190 --> 07:05.660
Really?

07:05.660 --> 07:08.250
I wasn't exactly angry.

07:08.250 --> 07:09.310
Were you not?

07:15.040 --> 07:17.440
This is so complicated.

07:21.330 --> 07:25.240
<i>A certain incident crossed my mind.</i>

07:29.070 --> 07:31.970
<i>That wasn't a mistake.</i>

07:32.350 --> 07:36.450
<i>But how do I make that clear?</i>

07:37.070 --> 07:39.300
Listen carefully to the sound.

07:39.700 --> 07:44.090
Play the third a little lower 
and the fifth slightly higher,

07:44.090 --> 07:45.950
and you'll get a crisp harmony.

07:46.430 --> 07:48.130
Keep that in mind.

07:48.130 --> 07:49.290
Right.

07:49.290 --> 07:50.430
Once more.

07:54.560 --> 07:56.240
What did I just say?

07:56.900 --> 07:58.720
Listen more carefully.

08:05.550 --> 08:06.680
Kumiko!

08:06.680 --> 08:07.980
Azusa-chan.

08:07.980 --> 08:09.660
What's with the weather today?

08:09.660 --> 08:10.750
Are you on your way home?

08:10.750 --> 08:11.880
Yeah.

08:11.880 --> 08:13.300
What about you?

08:13.300 --> 08:14.680
I have lessons.

08:14.680 --> 08:15.850
Yeah?

08:16.120 --> 08:18.590
Also, I haven't seen you since SunFes.

08:19.330 --> 08:20.350
Yeah.

08:20.920 --> 08:23.550
So, have you decided what you're 
doing after high school?

08:23.550 --> 08:25.400
I don't even have time.

08:25.400 --> 08:26.850
The competitions are coming up.

08:28.440 --> 08:30.360
Aren't your parents nagging you?

08:30.620 --> 08:32.380
Do you think they wouldn't?

08:33.630 --> 08:35.490
Why not music school, then?

08:35.490 --> 08:36.470
Here we go again.

08:36.470 --> 08:37.330
Again?

08:37.330 --> 08:39.990
Reina's been telling me the same thing.

08:39.990 --> 08:44.700
But it's not like I want to 
become a pro like Reina.

08:44.700 --> 08:46.660
She's an ultra-rare character.

08:46.660 --> 08:47.990
Do you think so, too?

08:48.300 --> 08:49.120
Isn't she?

08:49.490 --> 08:52.000
I'm shooting for music school, too,

08:52.000 --> 08:56.670
but I'm not really thinking about what 
I'm going to do after that like she is.

08:56.670 --> 08:58.140
Aren't you hoping to go pro?

08:58.560 --> 09:04.400
Ideally, I'd like to do 
something related to music.

09:06.200 --> 09:08.550
I never thought about things that way.

09:09.990 --> 09:14.390
If anything, wouldn't it be scarier 
to quit music cold turkey right now?

09:16.000 --> 09:16.990
Well...

09:17.600 --> 09:21.490
I hadn't thought about that, either.

09:21.490 --> 09:25.950
I don't know how much I love music,

09:25.950 --> 09:31.300
but I figure it might become something 
I want to do if I keep at it.

09:33.100 --> 09:35.030
Oh no, the time!

09:35.810 --> 09:37.150
I should go.

09:37.150 --> 09:38.100
Okay.

09:44.330 --> 09:45.130
Kumiko!

09:46.800 --> 09:48.770
Let me know what you decide.

09:48.770 --> 09:53.720
If you ask me, I can't picture 
you not doing music.

09:58.320 --> 10:04.870
<i>Time passed in the blink of an eye, 
and it was the day of the audition.</i>

10:05.160 --> 10:07.010
That was hopeless.

10:07.010 --> 10:08.770
I messed up.

10:08.770 --> 10:09.970
Nah.

10:09.970 --> 10:12.340
That was a good first attempt.

10:12.340 --> 10:13.280
Yeah.

10:13.280 --> 10:14.730
You had a good tone.

10:14.730 --> 10:16.260
No I didn't!

10:16.260 --> 10:17.350
I was so nervous.

10:17.350 --> 10:18.360
So you do get nervous?

10:18.360 --> 10:18.830
Yeah.

10:18.830 --> 10:23.080
And that drill sergeant of a teacher 
kept watching my fingers.

10:23.960 --> 10:26.430
The euphs are up soon.

10:26.430 --> 10:28.050
Don't be late.

10:28.050 --> 10:29.330
R-Right.

10:29.850 --> 10:31.230
I'm getting nervous.

10:31.230 --> 10:34.360
Relax. We're just doing this for next year.

10:34.360 --> 10:35.570
Come on...

10:36.190 --> 10:38.780
You won't know until you try.

10:38.780 --> 10:41.640
But the second and 
third-years are all so good.

10:41.640 --> 10:42.580
Err...

10:42.580 --> 10:46.560
You're doing the soli with 
Kousaka-senpai, too, aren't you?

10:46.560 --> 10:48.250
I'm looking forward to it!

10:50.420 --> 10:53.340
<b>Music Room</b>

10:51.140 --> 10:53.340
That was hopeless.

10:53.340 --> 10:55.300
Not at all.

10:55.300 --> 10:56.230
You had it.

10:56.230 --> 10:56.960
Really?

11:03.960 --> 11:05.220
Okay, that's enough.

11:08.200 --> 11:11.070
Next, the soli part, please.

11:11.070 --> 11:11.600
Okay.

11:12.510 --> 11:15.300
I wonder how many people are 
being picked for the euph part?

11:15.860 --> 11:17.060
I dunno.

11:17.060 --> 11:20.110
It depends on what Taki-sensei decides.

11:20.700 --> 11:21.610
Of course.

11:25.950 --> 11:30.920
<i>What would I do if </i>that<i> happens again?</i>

11:31.370 --> 11:33.000
<i>Would I stop them?</i>

11:33.750 --> 11:35.080
<i>Or...</i>

11:37.480 --> 11:39.920
Thanks for waiting, Kuroe-senpai.

11:39.920 --> 11:40.880
Please.

11:40.880 --> 11:41.690
Okay.

11:45.930 --> 11:47.210
Here I go.

11:47.210 --> 11:48.530
Good luck.

11:53.690 --> 11:56.730
I wonder what Kuroe-senpai's going to do.

11:56.730 --> 12:01.120
She could mess up on 
purpose so she drops out.

12:10.240 --> 12:11.630
She's good.

12:12.350 --> 12:13.140
Yeah.

12:13.740 --> 12:14.620
<i>I was relieved.</i>

12:15.620 --> 12:19.100
<i>It was the same beautiful sound as usual.</i>

12:23.310 --> 12:24.390
Kumiko-chan.

12:26.110 --> 12:26.870
Right.

12:27.680 --> 12:30.780
Well, Oumae-san, please start.

12:30.780 --> 12:31.770
Yes.

12:32.910 --> 12:34.500
<i>And for some reason...</i>

12:35.480 --> 12:37.060
<i>It motivated me.</i>

12:43.740 --> 12:44.990
Is something wrong?

12:46.590 --> 12:47.480
No.

12:48.980 --> 12:53.160
<i>This is my last year.</i>

13:00.290 --> 13:04.550
Unlike last year, we're going to have 
an audition for each competition.

13:04.550 --> 13:08.030
We'd like you to continue 
practicing for the competition,

13:08.030 --> 13:09.480
even if you aren't chosen this time.

13:11.980 --> 13:12.990
Pardon me.

13:12.990 --> 13:14.570
You were in the middle of speaking.

13:14.570 --> 13:15.720
No, go ahead, please.

13:15.720 --> 13:16.550
All right.

13:22.240 --> 13:25.700
I'm going to announce the 
members going to the Prefecturals.

13:25.700 --> 13:27.920
Respond when I call your name.

13:28.650 --> 13:30.610
First, trumpets.

13:31.550 --> 13:33.830
Third-year, Kousaka Reina.

13:34.520 --> 13:35.330
Yes.

13:35.330 --> 13:37.210
Second-year, Kohinata Yume.

13:37.210 --> 13:37.830
Yes.

13:38.230 --> 13:41.370
Trombones, third-year, Tsukamoto Shuichi.

13:41.370 --> 13:42.070
Yes.

13:42.450 --> 13:45.180
Oboe, second-year, Kenzaki Ririka.

13:45.180 --> 13:46.040
Yes.

13:46.510 --> 13:47.970
Next, euphoniums.

13:48.360 --> 13:50.550
Third-year, Oumae Kumiko.

13:50.550 --> 13:51.370
Yes.

13:51.370 --> 13:53.110
Third-year, Kuroe Mayu.

13:53.110 --> 13:53.840
Yes.

13:53.840 --> 13:55.850
Second-year, Hisaishi Kanade.

13:55.850 --> 13:56.610
Yes.

13:56.610 --> 13:57.910
That is all.

13:58.720 --> 14:00.310
Next, Tubas.

14:00.310 --> 14:02.230
Third-year, Katou Hazuki.

14:03.020 --> 14:04.340
Y-Yes.

14:08.980 --> 14:10.830
Second-year, Suzuki Mirei.

14:10.830 --> 14:11.740
Yes.

14:12.700 --> 14:15.070
First-year, Kamaya Suzume.

14:18.180 --> 14:19.630
Y-Yes.

14:19.630 --> 14:20.790
Those are our three tubas.

14:21.400 --> 14:22.880
Next, contrabass.

14:23.420 --> 14:25.330
Third-year, Kawashima Sapphire.

14:25.330 --> 14:26.080
Yes.

14:27.590 --> 14:30.260
Next, I'll announce our solo members.

14:31.350 --> 14:32.680
<b>Music Room</b>

14:31.860 --> 14:34.100
We did it, Hazuki-chan!

14:39.180 --> 14:40.380
Thanks.

14:40.380 --> 14:42.410
I can finally play in a competition.

14:42.410 --> 14:44.630
Onee-chan!

14:45.110 --> 14:48.480
You're playing in a competition 
as a first-year! I'm impressed.

14:48.480 --> 14:49.590
Praise me!

14:49.590 --> 14:50.700
Okay, okay.

14:58.120 --> 15:02.070
Underclassman, it isn't over yet.

15:02.070 --> 15:03.380
R-Right!

15:03.380 --> 15:04.320
Of course.

15:04.660 --> 15:06.530
It's just getting started.

15:06.530 --> 15:09.880
Kumiko-senpai, congratulations on the soli.

15:09.880 --> 15:10.900
Thanks.

15:10.900 --> 15:12.950
Let's make it a good performance together.

15:12.950 --> 15:14.120
Of course.

15:14.120 --> 15:15.850
I'm so glad.

15:16.510 --> 15:20.860
I was so worried it might 
be just the two of us.

15:20.860 --> 15:24.430
Do you mean you were 
expecting me to drop out?

15:24.430 --> 15:28.140
No, I just thought we wouldn't 
get more than two euphs

15:28.140 --> 15:30.100
for this arrangement.

15:30.100 --> 15:31.630
I see.

15:31.630 --> 15:34.070
So you think I was chosen out of pity.

15:33.480 --> 15:34.970
Kanade-chan.

15:35.340 --> 15:36.410
It's fine.

15:36.410 --> 15:40.760
I couldn't help myself. 
Kuroe-senpai is just such a nice person.

15:41.390 --> 15:44.950
Kaho-chan, you still have 
more chances. Good luck.

15:44.950 --> 15:46.090
Right.

15:46.880 --> 15:53.740
Though, to be honest, I'm happy just 
listening to my senpais play this year.

15:54.140 --> 15:55.480
Oumae-senpai.

15:55.800 --> 15:57.020
Micchan.

15:57.020 --> 15:59.070
Do you have a moment?

16:00.690 --> 16:05.070
To be honest, I don't understand 
how Satsuki could have failed.

16:05.400 --> 16:08.570
Suzume-chan just joined as a first-year.

16:08.570 --> 16:10.700
And she's a beginner, too.

16:10.700 --> 16:11.570
Yes.

16:11.570 --> 16:16.470
I agree that Kamaya-san 
sounds good for a beginner.

16:16.470 --> 16:20.700
But I don't think anyone would 
doubt that Satsuki is better.

16:20.700 --> 16:21.590
You're right.

16:22.380 --> 16:26.590
So you aren't satisfied with 
this result either, then?

16:29.200 --> 16:31.580
You hit me with the hard questions.

16:31.580 --> 16:33.140
Sorry.

16:33.140 --> 16:35.840
I was surprised, too.

16:36.520 --> 16:40.190
But I think Taki-sensei always 
thinks about the whole

16:40.190 --> 16:43.590
and plans things so that we 
have a good performance.

16:44.260 --> 16:47.990
I think we should trust his decision.

16:49.590 --> 16:50.890
Understood.

16:52.070 --> 16:52.850
You're fine with that?

16:53.260 --> 16:57.670
It's not like I want to start trouble 
right before the competition.

16:58.600 --> 17:01.840
If that's how you feel, I'll trust him, too.

17:01.840 --> 17:03.490
Really?

17:03.730 --> 17:04.280
But...

17:05.620 --> 17:09.710
Unlike the third-years who've been 
studying with him all this time,

17:10.280 --> 17:14.130
the first and second-years don't 
revere him the same way.

17:14.650 --> 17:17.210
I just want you to keep that in mind.

17:19.480 --> 17:20.620
All right.

17:20.620 --> 17:21.830
Thanks.

17:22.180 --> 17:24.170
Why are you thanking me?

17:25.420 --> 17:30.080
It's rare that my underclassmen 
ever give me their opinions.

17:30.080 --> 17:32.990
Please tell me if there's ever 
anything bothering you again.

17:33.610 --> 17:34.450
Right.

17:36.750 --> 17:39.140
<i>An audition for each competition.</i>

17:39.710 --> 17:42.720
<i>And each time, there's 
apprehension and anger.</i>

17:43.170 --> 17:46.250
<i>I have to quell that and 
keep everyone together.</i>

17:46.900 --> 17:50.280
<i>The thought of it weighed 
heavily on my chest.</i>

17:57.520 --> 17:59.190
<i>I have to calm down.</i>

18:07.270 --> 18:08.270
Sound! Euphonium

18:34.590 --> 18:35.870
Mayu-chan.

18:37.370 --> 18:38.480
Sorry.

18:38.480 --> 18:39.910
Am I interrupting?

18:39.910 --> 18:40.930
No.

18:40.930 --> 18:43.830
What's wrong? Do you not 
have a spot to practice?

18:43.830 --> 18:44.940
No, no.

18:44.940 --> 18:49.400
It's just that I heard pretty euphonium 
sounds, so I thought it might be you.

18:49.730 --> 18:50.880
What's that piece?

18:51.740 --> 18:53.390
The one you were just playing.

18:54.360 --> 18:57.220
It's nothing worth sharing.

18:57.220 --> 19:00.320
I was just playing for fun.

19:02.370 --> 19:05.040
Is it something you composed?

19:05.360 --> 19:06.600
Of course not.

19:06.600 --> 19:09.050
Someone told me about this piece.

19:09.050 --> 19:10.170
Really?

19:10.170 --> 19:11.150
Your senpai?

19:12.780 --> 19:13.750
I guess.

19:15.410 --> 19:16.040
Sorry.

19:16.470 --> 19:18.000
I guess I am interrupting.

19:18.000 --> 19:19.370
I'll go practice, too.

19:24.360 --> 19:26.540
<i>I didn't want to tell her for some reason.</i>

19:27.410 --> 19:31.360
<i>I felt resistant to being known.</i>

19:29.980 --> 19:30.600
Sound! Euphonium

19:32.050 --> 19:33.090
<i>Especially...</i>

19:37.110 --> 19:39.110
I'm going to return the key

19:37.110 --> 19:39.110
You have lessons, right, Reina?

19:39.680 --> 19:41.110
Excuse me.

19:41.110 --> 19:45.120
<b>Staff Office</b>

19:41.820 --> 19:44.020
Everyone's left, right?

19:44.020 --> 19:45.130
Yes.

19:45.130 --> 19:46.760
I think it'll be fine.

19:47.790 --> 19:49.240
What's the matter?

19:50.320 --> 19:51.260
Um...

19:51.260 --> 19:52.080
Yes?

19:52.920 --> 19:55.400
About the audition...

19:55.400 --> 19:59.290
Ah, Matsumoto-sensei made 
the announcement, correct?

19:59.290 --> 20:00.200
Yes.

20:00.620 --> 20:03.820
I have a question about that.

20:03.820 --> 20:04.760
What is it?

20:06.250 --> 20:10.460
I don't know if this is something 
I should be asking...

20:10.460 --> 20:12.640
But the choice for tuba...

20:12.640 --> 20:14.530
Kamaya-san, correct?

20:15.720 --> 20:16.910
I mean...

20:16.910 --> 20:21.520
Compared to Sacchan, she's, err...

20:23.480 --> 20:30.860
What were your criteria when you 
voted for the club ensemble contest?

20:32.140 --> 20:33.300
Well...

20:33.690 --> 20:36.130
Polish, I guess?

20:36.550 --> 20:38.820
Same for me.

20:39.560 --> 20:44.030
It's true that Kamaya-san is clumsy, 
but she has magnificent sound.

20:44.440 --> 20:49.710
I felt that her sound was desirable 
for the balance of the whole.

20:49.710 --> 20:52.700
But it isn't just about being loud, is it?

20:52.700 --> 20:54.270
That's correct.

20:54.760 --> 21:01.660
But when we're performing with a limited 
group, loudness is quite important.

21:02.210 --> 21:07.020
We can simply have her not play the 
high notes or other difficult parts.

21:09.490 --> 21:12.190
Um, err...

21:12.920 --> 21:17.740
You're taking us to the Nationals, right?

21:19.460 --> 21:22.610
That's not the correct framing.

21:22.610 --> 21:24.890
You're going with your own abilities.

21:27.350 --> 21:28.680
I'm sorry.

21:30.490 --> 21:33.380
I look forward to the euphonium soli.

21:34.280 --> 21:35.930
Pardon me.

21:35.930 --> 21:36.850
Kumiko.

21:38.080 --> 21:38.850
Reina.

21:39.320 --> 21:41.540
Why are you here this late?

21:42.320 --> 21:45.470
I was talking to my homeroom 
teacher about my career path.

21:45.470 --> 21:47.250
Yeah? What about it?

21:47.250 --> 21:49.810
Never mind that.

21:49.810 --> 21:51.860
What were you discussing with Taki-sensei?

21:51.860 --> 21:54.120
You were there without the 
drum major and vice president.

21:54.120 --> 21:56.450
You should have come in.

21:56.860 --> 21:59.540
I don't even have a reason. I couldn't.

21:59.540 --> 22:01.840
It's not a big deal.

22:01.840 --> 22:03.790
We were just discussing the Prefecturals.

22:03.790 --> 22:05.630
What's the problem?

22:03.800 --> 22:06.800
Congrats
Kansai 
Competition
 Boys'
 High
 School
Broadcast
 Contest
 Announcement
 Team

22:06.790 --> 22:09.420
Anyway, congratulations on making the soli.

22:10.670 --> 22:11.440
Yeah.

22:11.440 --> 22:16.200
I'm hoping the two of us do the 
soli together up to the Nationals.

22:16.200 --> 22:17.180
Yeah.

22:17.590 --> 22:21.400
I'm certain we'll get gold 
in the Nationals that way.

22:21.400 --> 22:22.910
We have Taki-sensei, too.

22:22.910 --> 22:24.410
Taki-sensei...

22:26.600 --> 22:27.980
Nah.

22:28.370 --> 22:31.020
And we have our scary drum major, too.

22:31.330 --> 22:34.800
And the president who's buddies 
with that drum major.

22:37.960 --> 22:42.410
<i>We're definitely going to run 
into problems going forward.</i>

22:39.830 --> 22:48.300
<i><b>Kyoto Concert Band Prefectural Competition
(Kansai Concert Band Competition Kyoto Preliminaries)</b></i>

22:43.320 --> 22:50.370
<i>But all we can do is believe, 
and keep playing towards our goal.</i>

22:52.730 --> 22:57.620
All our hardships and difficult 
practice were for today.

22:58.820 --> 23:02.460
Let's do our best so that 
we're left with no regrets.

23:02.460 --> 23:03.200
Yes.

23:04.090 --> 23:05.090
President.

23:11.330 --> 23:14.700
Go, Kitauji!

23:19.430 --> 23:23.570
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>

23:22.000 --> 23:25.960
<b>To be continued</b>
